(608753, 62594, 16269, '<td valign="top">I love this shot! It screams silence (hehe.. little bit of an oxymoron, there. I suppose I should say that it whispers silence!). I love the colors and the angle. This is one of my very most favorite photos in this challenge.</td>', 'I love this shot! It screams silence (hehe.. little bit of an oxymoron, there. I suppose I should say that it whispers silence!). I love the colors and the angle. This is one of my very most favorite photos in this challenge.', '2004-03-04 00:11:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(608754, 62830, 16269, '<td valign="top">Wow.. this picture really shows silence, but in a creepy sort of way. I really like the yellowness of it. It definitely portrays silence.. but a kind of silence that would give me the chills if I was out there alone. Nice job!</td>', 'Wow.. this picture really shows silence, but in a creepy sort of way. I really like the yellowness of it. It definitely portrays silence.. but a kind of silence that would give me the chills if I was out there alone. Nice job!', '2004-03-04 00:12:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(608759, 62590, 16269, '<td valign="top">You know.. there were quite a few evening and landscape shots in this challenge and I really wasn''t impressed with most of them. They were pretty, sure, but just not very dynamic, in my opinion. However.. when I came across your photo, I just sat and stared. It''s beautiful. I love the very tiny hint of sunset, and the silhouettes of the trees, but also the touch of fences against snow. The little "scratch" in the sky is unfortunate but... as many things as you can control in photography, you can''t control nature! Maybe you would edit that out, if you were to make a print. I''m not really sure (I''m new to all of this!) Lovely job! One of my favorites in the entire challenge!<br/> <br/>edit - (Uncoftunate was really unfortunate.. wow.. odd spelling, I have. Fixed it! After the challenge, this is still one of my favorite shots.)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-03-10 00:08:40.</i></td>', 'You know.. there were quite a few evening and landscape shots in this challenge and I really wasn''t impressed with most of them. They were pretty, sure, but just not very dynamic, in my opinion. However.. when I came across your photo, I just sat and stared. It''s beautiful. I love the very tiny hint of sunset, and the silhouettes of the trees, but also the touch of fences against snow. The little "scratch" in the sky is unfortunate but... as many things as you can control in photography, you can''t control nature! Maybe you would edit that out, if you were to make a print. I''m not really sure (I''m new to all of this!) Lovely job! One of my favorites in the entire challenge! edit - (Uncoftunate was really unfortunate.. wow.. odd spelling, I have. Fixed it! After the challenge, this is still one of my favorite shots.)', '2004-03-04 00:22:10.000000', '2004-03-10 00:08:40.000000', 1),
(608767, 62677, 12712, '<td valign="top">I love the idea, and the entire shot in general.  My only 10</td>', 'I love the idea, and the entire shot in general.  My only 10', '2004-03-04 00:43:04.000000', NULL, 1);
