(612490, 62708, 3746, '<td valign="top">This is a truely great photograph.. I dont think its fair they let professional photographers, such as yourself, enter amateur competitions such as this. The silence in this photo SCREAMS at me. The inquisitive look of the faux bird, cast in lifelike plastic is not only joyous to behold, but touches me in a deep spiritual way. The stony stare of the feline tells of pent up agressive, waiting to unleash his fury upon an unsuspecting world. To mark this picture as a ten would be an injustice to its raw beauty, so to make a statement, I will give it a 2, but rest assured that in my heart, it will always be a winner..</td>', 'This is a truely great photograph.. I dont think its fair they let professional photographers, such as yourself, enter amateur competitions such as this. The silence in this photo SCREAMS at me. The inquisitive look of the faux bird, cast in lifelike plastic is not only joyous to behold, but touches me in a deep spiritual way. The stony stare of the feline tells of pent up agressive, waiting to unleash his fury upon an unsuspecting world. To mark this picture as a ten would be an injustice to its raw beauty, so to make a statement, I will give it a 2, but rest assured that in my heart, it will always be a winner..', '2004-03-07 04:16:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(612491, 62927, 15164, '<td valign="top">i like the geometric component of this image.. great composition with a lot of different textures and colors.. very nice shot..</td>', 'i like the geometric component of this image.. great composition with a lot of different textures and colors.. very nice shot..', '2004-03-07 04:16:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(612493, 62250, 10084, '<td valign="top">What an intese look from your subject. The composition is perfect. Really like seeing the books behind. Give a hint of location. The add book with "Hellen Keller" adds an extra bit of interesting. Great combination of contrast and brightness."10"</td>', 'What an intese look from your subject. The composition is perfect. Really like seeing the books behind. Give a hint of location. The add book with "Hellen Keller" adds an extra bit of interesting. Great combination of contrast and brightness."10"', '2004-03-07 04:23:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(612494, 62654, 10084, '<td valign="top">Excellent composition and setup of the bear. The angle fo the head and the placement of the paw really gives a sense of silence. The lighting from the top of the bear brings out the gurry texture of the subject. That highlight glare in the eyes adds the finishing touch. Nice simple design. "10"</td>', 'Excellent composition and setup of the bear. The angle fo the head and the placement of the paw really gives a sense of silence. The lighting from the top of the bear brings out the gurry texture of the subject. That highlight glare in the eyes adds the finishing touch. Nice simple design. "10"', '2004-03-07 04:25:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(612495, 63121, 3746, '<td valign="top">ARRRRGGGGGHHH, this is so damn fraustrating...<br/>OK, lets start with the good and positive.. FANTASTIC PHOTO!! I love the simplicity of it, it worked well on my screen as I could only see the top 2 thirds of the pic, I didnt know what to expect as I scrolled down, and the green feather just.... well, worked! I am about mid way through voting and this will easily reach top ten, maybe top five??<br/>OK, now onto the negative.. DONT RELY ON A TITLE TO MAKE A PICTURE FIT THE CHALLENGE! The pics I usually rate highest would not need a title, they would scream SILENCE out to me (is that something of a contradiction in terms?), granted they would be technically good as well, but I am from the old school of DPChallenge, where I think subject should be adhered to, not there as an afterthought. I oh so want to give this a ten, I really do, I love minimilistic work.. Oh f**k it, have a nine this time but take my comments on board.... Nince one!!!  9 marksimms</td>', 'ARRRRGGGGGHHH, this is so damn fraustrating...OK, lets start with the good and positive.. FANTASTIC PHOTO!! I love the simplicity of it, it worked well on my screen as I could only see the top 2 thirds of the pic, I didnt know what to expect as I scrolled down, and the green feather just.... well, worked! I am about mid way through voting and this will easily reach top ten, maybe top five??OK, now onto the negative.. DONT RELY ON A TITLE TO MAKE A PICTURE FIT THE CHALLENGE! The pics I usually rate highest would not need a title, they would scream SILENCE out to me (is that something of a contradiction in terms?), granted they would be technically good as well, but I am from the old school of DPChallenge, where I think subject should be adhered to, not there as an afterthought. I oh so want to give this a ten, I really do, I love minimilistic work.. Oh f**k it, have a nine this time but take my comments on board.... Nince one!!!  9 marksimms', '2004-03-07 04:25:40.000000', NULL, 1),
