(616793, 62237, 17578, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the constructive comments.  Gpierson''s comment was wonderful, I will try the lamp.  Rasal your Mom could probably teach this Cairn to talk he is a great pet and smart dog. It was small because I didn''t have software that allowed me to change it properly...I have figured that problem out using some great shareware I found.<br/> <br/>I only take the pictures as a hobby  and a friend really liked some of the pictures I have of Rebel.  He is a great subject and I have some fun pictures of him. For those of you who can''t see the detail...he looks like red version of Toto in the Wizard of Oz.</td>', 'Thanks for all the constructive comments.  Gpierson''s comment was wonderful, I will try the lamp.  Rasal your Mom could probably teach this Cairn to talk he is a great pet and smart dog. It was small because I didn''t have software that allowed me to change it properly...I have figured that problem out using some great shareware I found. I only take the pictures as a hobby  and a friend really liked some of the pictures I have of Rebel.  He is a great subject and I have some fun pictures of him. For those of you who can''t see the detail...he looks like red version of Toto in the Wizard of Oz.', '2004-03-10 12:55:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(616795, 62248, 5391, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club! <br/> <br/>Composition: For the most part, I like the composition.  You''ve got nice dynamic lines that keep the eye in the image.  I think that perhaps the dark three dimensional object that grows out of focus as it gets nearer the camera is a bit too prominent in the image, however.  Perhaps with greater depth of field, if the entire object was sharp and in focus, it wouldn''t be so distracting.  It keeps distracting me from the interesting details and textures of the wet paper.  I do, however, like the monotone feel of the image.<br/> <br/>Challenge: I''m not sure that this says "silence" to me - it invokes the feeling of an urban street, which I associate with noise.<br/> <br/>Camera Work: Very nice - sharp where it needs to be, appears to have been taken using a tripod. Exposure is very good, excellent tonal range that would also make it work well as a toned image or black and white.<br/> <br/>My Opinion: Overall, I like this image.  Particularly the feeling of dampness - it''s a very "arty" shot.  I can see it as part of a series hanging in a gallery.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Composition: For the most part, I like the composition.  You''ve got nice dynamic lines that keep the eye in the image.  I think that perhaps the dark three dimensional object that grows out of focus as it gets nearer the camera is a bit too prominent in the image, however.  Perhaps with greater depth of field, if the entire object was sharp and in focus, it wouldn''t be so distracting.  It keeps distracting me from the interesting details and textures of the wet paper.  I do, however, like the monotone feel of the image. Challenge: I''m not sure that this says "silence" to me - it invokes the feeling of an urban street, which I associate with noise. Camera Work: Very nice - sharp where it needs to be, appears to have been taken using a tripod. Exposure is very good, excellent tonal range that would also make it work well as a toned image or black and white. My Opinion: Overall, I like this image.  Particularly the feeling of dampness - it''s a very "arty" shot.  I can see it as part of a series hanging in a gallery.', '2004-03-10 12:56:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(616800, 63021, 5391, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club! <br/> <br/>Composition: Excellent composition.  Wonderful use of space.  Depth of field is perfect, clearly showing the artist and his instrument.  The capture of the expression of the musician is wonderful and complemented nicely by the warm lighting.  I really get a feeling of warmth and peacefulness from this image.  The only thing I would like is a touch of unsharp mask - I suspect that when you resized this it got a little soft, and I would love to see tiny details in the man''s face, like eyelashes, etc.  I think that would really make it "pop" off the screen.<br/> <br/>Challenge: You''ve met the challenge criteria extremely well.  The feeling of silence that this conveys is wonderful.<br/> <br/>My Opinion: Overall, I really like this.  It''s hard to capture mood so well in a photo, especially with people.  I''m a bit curious to know if he was modeling for you or if you somehow grabbed this shot candidly.  Either way, it''s a beautiful portrait of a musician.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Composition: Excellent composition.  Wonderful use of space.  Depth of field is perfect, clearly showing the artist and his instrument.  The capture of the expression of the musician is wonderful and complemented nicely by the warm lighting.  I really get a feeling of warmth and peacefulness from this image.  The only thing I would like is a touch of unsharp mask - I suspect that when you resized this it got a little soft, and I would love to see tiny details in the man''s face, like eyelashes, etc.  I think that would really make it "pop" off the screen. Challenge: You''ve met the challenge criteria extremely well.  The feeling of silence that this conveys is wonderful. My Opinion: Overall, I really like this.  It''s hard to capture mood so well in a photo, especially with people.  I''m a bit curious to know if he was modeling for you or if you somehow grabbed this shot candidly.  Either way, it''s a beautiful portrait of a musician. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.', '2004-03-10 13:04:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(616819, 62694, 7435, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for the comments. Many of you said too dark. I chose the slightly underexposed pic too add to the silence.</td>', 'Thank you all for the comments. Many of you said too dark. I chose the slightly underexposed pic too add to the silence.', '2004-03-10 13:24:28.000000', NULL, 0),
